# Narrator: Into the Mists (into_the_mists_road). Voice: docs/voice/narrator.md.

# --- The location -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~ enter:into_the_mists_road
| The fog behind you thickens like a door swinging shut. The road ahead runs west, under trees that lean in to listen.
| [flag.death_house_completed] The road east ends where it always did, in a wall of mist that does not care what you survived.
| [flag.mists_wolves_resolved] Back on the Old Svalich Road, where the trees are still leaning in. They have heard about you.
cooldown 60

# --- Areas ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~ enter:mists_svalich_woods
| Pines crowd the road, black against a sky the color of old pewter. Somewhere off to the left, a wolf howls, and somewhere to the right, another answers.
| [species:elf] {name} knows old forests. This one is old the way a grudge is old.
| [class:ranger] {name} counts the howls, six from three directions, and they are not hunting. They are herding.
once

~ enter:mists_gates
| A pair of tall iron gates bars the road, kept by two stone knights who have lost their heads but not their posts. The gates are shut, and the road goes through them anyway.
| [flag.mists_wolves_cowed] The pack let you pass, and the woods have gone very quiet about it. Ahead, a wall of stone and a gate of iron.
| [flag.mists_wolves_fought] Wolf blood dries on your boots. Ahead, two headless stone knights keep a gate that seems to be expecting you.
once

~ enter:mists_village_edge
| Shuttered cottages, mud, and woodsmoke from chimneys that are trying not to be noticed. A village, at last, holding its breath.
| [class:rogue] {name} notes every shutter barred from the inside. Nobody here is keeping thieves out; they're keeping something else out.
once

# --- Props ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~ examine:mists_wall
| White, cold and patient. The road you came in on is somewhere inside it, and the mist would rather you didn't go looking.
| [class:wizard] The fog hums very faintly, like a held note. Whatever made it is still making it.

~ examine:mists_signpost
| A signpost leans over the road. One arm says Barovia; the other, pointing back the way you came, has been sawn off.
| [tag:curious] Someone carved a tally of marks into the post, dozens of them, and then stopped. {name} decides not to wonder why.

~ examine:mists_deer_carcass
| A deer, torn open and left. Whatever killed it didn't stay to eat.

~ examine:mists_wayside_shrine
| A little roadside shrine, its sun-disk chipped away to bare stone. Someone still leaves candle stubs here, though none of them are lit.
| [class:cleric] A shrine to the Morninglord, defaced but not abandoned. {name} sets the sun-disk straight; it keeps sliding back.

~ examine:gate_statues
| Two stone knights stand guard with grounded swords. Their heads are gone, broken off clean at the neck, and they keep watch anyway.
| [flag.mists_gates_opened] The gates stand open now. Neither of the headless knights looks pleased about it.

~ search:gate_heads
| Half-buried in the weeds: two stone heads, faces worn smooth by weather, both turned to look back down the road.

~ check:perception:gate_heads:success
| {name} kicks aside the weeds at the foot of the gate and finds a stone face looking back up.

~ check:perception:gate_heads:failure
| Weeds, rubble and fog. The gate keeps its own counsel.

~ examine:edge_cottage_shutters
| The shutters are barred, but a candle burns behind them. When you look closer, it goes out.

~ examine:edge_alley_crow
| A crow sits on a rain barrel and watches you with professional interest.
| [species:halfling] The crow looks {name} up and down, plainly deciding whether {name} counts as a snack.

~ open:barovia_gates
| The gates swing open before anyone touches them, slow and silent on hinges that should be screaming with rust.
once

~ open:abandoned_cart
| A cart on its side, one wheel gone. Its owner left in a hurry, and not on the cart.
once

# --- Traps ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~ trap:mists_wolf_trap:found
| There, under the leaves: the iron teeth of a wolf trap, set right in the road.
| [class:ranger] {name} spots the trap's chain staked into the verge. A hunter set this for wolves, and the wolves know it's here.

~ trap:mists_wolf_trap:triggered
| Iron jaws snap shut on a boot. Somewhere in the fog, a wolf yips, almost like laughter.

~ trap:mists_wolf_trap:disarmed
| The trap's jaws close slowly on a stick. Its spring sighs, disappointed.

# --- Hidden finds (docs/story/found_magic_items.md) ---

~ search:mists_guard_sword
| A sword lies in the weeds below the headless statues, and its blade is bright, as if no rain has ever touched it. Whoever kept this gate dropped it and did not come back.
once

~ check:perception:mists_guard_sword:failure
| Weeds, mud and broken stone. Something glints, or doesn't; the mist won't say.

~ search:mists_shrine_board
| One board at the back of the shrine is newer than the rest. Under it, wrapped in oilcloth, a glass orb whose little cloud always drifts the same way: north.
once

~ check:investigation:mists_shrine_board:failure
| The shrine is old and the boards are older. If it hides anything, it hides it well.
